{"author":{"id":"d4d77c46d796577aec35d160aa1e09aa095720b03e93f3ca34ad3c079140e2fb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794731232,"nonce":"M0FwNe6ChbGOouL94BkQ+KdZ3mo=","title":"A driver cannot add fields to a shader class","message":"`Build.native` decides every field a shader class gets. A GPU driver built on hxnsl cannot add its own, such as a prebuilt pipeline descriptor, a `.metallib` resource and its accessor, or a typed bind group helper, and cannot leave out the fields it does not use. `-D hxnsl_targets` chooses targets for the whole compilation, not for one shader family, so two frameworks in one program cannot choose differently.","files":null}]}